// endpoint_update_classifier_prompt.proto — UpdateClassifierPrompt: a held
// card's "update classifier" control. HELD TRAY section.
//
// A prompt the routing classifier held (interject, after this tool call, or
// wait for the turn's end) offers the reader a way to change HOW the
// classifier decides: they say the change in their own words, and the DAEMON
// has a headless model rewrite the routing brief
// (`prompts/queue-routing-classifier.md`) to carry it, then COMMITS that one
// file. The next classification reads the rewritten brief, since every brief
// is read at use time.
//
// DAEMON-GLOBAL, NOT PER-WORKSPACE. There is one routing brief per daemon, so
// the request names no workspace: the card it was asked from contributes only
// the worked example the rewrite is shown.
//
// ONLY THAT CHANGE, ONLY THAT FILE. The daemon refuses to rewrite a brief
// that already carries uncommitted edits, and it commits the brief's path
// alone, so the commit holds exactly the rewrite and nothing else staged in
// the checkout. A rewrite that would break the brief (a placeholder lost or
// invented, an empty body) is refused before anything is written, and a
// commit that fails puts the file back the way it was.

